  "verdict": "SMOKE-VALIDATED (machinery + wall-#1 handling) -- the pipeline runs end-to-end on a real SimulationBridge; the recurrent synapses MOVE under the committed BDSP rule (plastic mean|dw| 0.04019 > 0.0001); the DIRECTED apical credit is ISOLABLE in the soma_g sweep -- at g=0 (decoupled) B stays 0 and directed==lesion (the documented boundary), and turning on bdsp_apical_couples_soma raises measured bursts B monotonically with g and steers the weight move up to 12.4x the apical=0 lesion. LESION-BUG FIX (this build): the arm was named 'apical_lesion' but the teach checked mode=='lesion' -> the lesion ran the FULL directed apical (== plastic); corrected to a TRUE apical=0 lesion. With it, the CORRECTED apical_lesion arm (apical=0) shows the DIRECTED credit DOMINATES the undirected -Pbar*E drift (plastic directed |dw| 0.03491 = plastic 0.04019 - lesion 0.00528, ~6.6x the undirected drift), and the drift is METRIC-INERT (lesion CE 1.461 ~ fixed 1.462) -- so plastic is NOT swamped by drift; it moves the weights in the credited direction but that reservoir change yields only a MARGINAL read-out CE gain (plastic 1.437 vs fixed 1.462) at this scale. A clean within-horizon CE-win still needs the sparser bursting regime + lr/epoch tuning = the controller's sweep. NOT a faked positive."
